        "node_id": "n_1_6fe988",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of iterating year by year is inefficient for large values of X, leading to a timeout. Instead, we can use the mathematical formula for compound interest to calculate the number of years directly. This approach will be much faster and avoid precision issues with floating-point calculations.",
